This project was carried out as part of the fourth practical phase, from 29.06.2026 to 28.08.2026, at Hitachi Energy The Netherlands B.V. in Rotterdam, in the Engineering department, under the guidance of the company supervisor Marco Van-Rosmalen.

#acrl("CT") play a crucial role in power system protection, making accurate and reliable calculation methods essential for engineering practice. With the increasing use of software tools in protection engineering, the validation and assessment of automated calculations become increasingly important.

The objective of this project is to evaluate the quality of #acrs("CT") calculations performed by SECP Global. To achieve this, the software results are compared with independent reference calculations and assessed using a structured quality assessment approach. The work combines theoretical aspects of protection engineering with practical challenges encountered in an industrial environment.

I would like to express my sincere gratitude to my supervisors and colleagues at Hitachi Energy for their valuable support, expertise and constructive feedback throughout this project. I would also like to thank my academic supervisors at DHBW for their guidance and support.
